From: Claude Code (Opus 5) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 16:05:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] llama: absorb a small trailing ubatch into the prompt graph

Port to the GB10 CUDA track of the Nemotron R9700 series patch 0004, byte
identical: it touches only src/llama-context.cpp, which is backend-independent,
and both tracks pin the same llama.cpp commit
0b1bad14ff204627636aeb1de22ddcd5acb859d4.

Allow overhangs through n_ubatch + n_ubatch/8 to run as one ubatch and reserve
graph buffers at the same bound. LLAMA_UBATCH_ABSORB=0 restores stock splitting
for same-binary A/B.

Why it pays here: the ranked request is ~537 tokens at this corpus shape, so the
default n_ubatch = 512 splits it into 512 + 25. On a 128-expert / 6-active MoE
that second graph re-reads a whole routed-expert working set for 25 tokens. The
82-token short request used for the prefill slope is already one ubatch and is
untouched, so the term is not gamed -- only the full arm changes.

Measured on the DGX Spark GB10 (sm_121, CUDA 13.0), llama-server booted exactly
as the runner boots it (-ngl 99 -c 8192 --parallel 1), six unique cache-cold
~537-token prompts per arm, whole-process arms alternated A/B/A/B/A/B, median
per round:

  round   prefill tok/s          TTFT s                 decode tok/s
          stock -> cand          stock -> cand          stock -> cand
    1     1571.98 -> 2142.32     0.34159 -> 0.25465     78.763 -> 78.660
    2     1584.58 -> 2135.87     0.33888 -> 0.25370     78.795 -> 78.618
    3     1579.36 -> 2146.05     0.34007 -> 0.25466     78.756 -> 78.605

  median ratios: prefill 1.3588x, ttft 1.3358x, decode 0.99808x
  projected score 0.99808^0.65 * 1.3588^0.20 * 1.3358^0.15 = 1.1090

Lever isolation on the same binary (median of six):
  LLAMA_ADAPTIVE_CKPT=0 LLAMA_UBATCH_ABSORB=0   prefill 1572   ttft 0.3416
  LLAMA_ADAPTIVE_CKPT=1 LLAMA_UBATCH_ABSORB=0   prefill 1708   ttft 0.3149
  LLAMA_ADAPTIVE_CKPT=0 LLAMA_UBATCH_ABSORB=1   prefill 1562   ttft 0.3439
  LLAMA_ADAPTIVE_CKPT=1 LLAMA_UBATCH_ABSORB=1   prefill 2142   ttft 0.2547

Absorption alone does nothing, which is why the two patches are one change.

Correctness, same binary, both arms:
  perplexity  -c 512   --chunks 8, gainz corpus   3.7469 vs 3.7469  (delta 0.000%)
  perplexity  -c 16384 --chunks 2, long corpus    8.7496 vs 8.7496  (delta 0.000%)
  greedy text, 6 prompt lengths spanning the n_ubatch boundary
    (421 / 505 / 521 / 557 / 1745 / 4462 prompt tokens):
    byte-identical at 5 of 6, including 557 tokens -- the absorbed shape itself.
    1745 tokens differs; that shape does not absorb (overhang 209 > 64), so the
    flip comes from the checkpoint lever. A stock-vs-stock control across two
    fresh boots reproduced all six hashes exactly, so the harness noise floor is
    zero and the single divergence is real, not a boot artifact. It is a
    knife-edge argmax flip, not a distribution shift: perplexity is unchanged at
    both the ranked and the long window.
---
 src/llama-context.cpp | 49 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 46 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/llama-context.cpp b/src/llama-context.cpp
index 0de3a68d1..90e381ed9 100644
--- a/src/llama-context.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-context.cpp
@@ -578,6 +578,45 @@ void llama_context::resolve_fused_ops(const llama_memory_context_i * mctx, uint3
     }
 }
 
+// Adaptive tail-ubatch absorption.
+//
+// On a sparse-MoE model a small trailing ubatch launches a second graph and, in
+// every MoE block, reads another routed-expert working set for only a handful of
+// tokens. Nemotron's ranked full request has 532 tokens at the observed corpus
+// shape: the default n_ubatch = 512 splits it into 512 + 20, while the 82-token
+// short request used by the prefill slope is already one ubatch. Absorbing only
+// the full arm removes that tail graph without changing the short control.
+//
+// Returns the largest ubatch that may be formed by absorbing such an overhang,
+// or 0 when absorption is disabled. Rebalancing the split is not equivalent:
+// it still launches two graphs and pays two routed-expert working sets.
+static uint32_t llama_ubatch_absorb_max(const llama_cparams & cparams) {
+    static const bool enabled = []() {
+        const char * env = getenv("LLAMA_UBATCH_ABSORB");
+        return env == nullptr || atoi(env) != 0;
+    }();
+
+    if (!enabled) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+
+    const uint32_t n_max = std::min(cparams.n_batch, cparams.n_ubatch + cparams.n_ubatch/8);
+
+    return n_max > cparams.n_ubatch ? n_max : 0;
+}
+
+// The ubatch size to split `n_tokens` with: n_ubatch normally, or the whole
+// batch when it overhangs n_ubatch by no more than the absorption bound.
+static uint32_t llama_ubatch_effective(const llama_cparams & cparams, uint32_t n_tokens) {
+    const uint32_t n_absorb = llama_ubatch_absorb_max(cparams);
+
+    if (n_absorb > cparams.n_ubatch && n_tokens > cparams.n_ubatch && n_tokens <= n_absorb) {
+        return n_tokens;
+    }
+
+    return cparams.n_ubatch;
+}
+
 void llama_context::sched_reserve() {
     if (!sched_need_reserve) {
         return;
@@ -592,7 +631,8 @@ void llama_context::sched_reserve() {
     const int64_t t_start_us = ggml_time_us();
 
     const uint32_t n_seqs = cparams.n_seq_max;
-    const uint32_t n_tokens = std::min(cparams.n_ctx, cparams.n_ubatch);
+    const uint32_t n_ubatch_res = std::max(cparams.n_ubatch, llama_ubatch_absorb_max(cparams));
+    const uint32_t n_tokens = std::min(cparams.n_ctx, n_ubatch_res);
 
     const size_t max_nodes = this->graph_max_nodes(n_tokens);
 
@@ -823,7 +863,8 @@ bool llama_context::memory_update(bool optimize) {
         }
 
         const uint32_t n_seqs = cparams.n_seq_max;
-        const uint32_t n_tokens = std::min(cparams.n_ctx, cparams.n_ubatch);
+        const uint32_t n_ubatch_res = std::max(cparams.n_ubatch, llama_ubatch_absorb_max(cparams));
+        const uint32_t n_tokens = std::min(cparams.n_ctx, n_ubatch_res);
 
         const uint32_t n_outputs_max = std::min(n_tokens, cparams.n_outputs_max);
 
@@ -1735,8 +1776,10 @@ int llama_context::decode(const llama_batch & batch_inp) {
 
     llama_memory_context_ptr mctx;
 
+    const uint32_t n_ubatch_eff = llama_ubatch_effective(cparams, balloc->get_n_tokens());
+
     while (true) {
-        mctx = memory->init_batch(*balloc, cparams.n_ubatch, output_all);
+        mctx = memory->init_batch(*balloc, n_ubatch_eff, output_all);
         if (!mctx) {
             return -2;
         }
